<!-- One number — flow mode. The figures come from reverse-engineering a single card-grid slide from
     a corporate deck by rebuilding it in python-pptx. The left panel shows that cost (128); the right
     panel shows the same picture as one line of SOML — float a lone number in the middle and the
     audience asks "128 compared to what?". Both panels take the full height below the heading through
     the stretch of a `grow="1"` grid.

     The strip at the bottom of the left panel makes you count 128 with your eyes: two bars of the
     same width overlaid, one drawn as 128 vertical hatch lines (`pattern(vertical …)`), the other as
     a single cell. The right panel is a gradient of two accents the theme owns — color, not a number,
     points to "this side". The text on it is `bg`, so it contrasts with the accents in any theme
     (accents are chosen at 4.5:1 or better against the background). -->
<slide id="cost" enter="rise">
  <text variant="kicker">Rebuilding one card-grid slide from a corporate deck in python-pptx</text>
  <grid cols="3fr 2fr" gap="lg" grow="1">
    <shape variant="card" type="rounded-rect" w="fill" pad="lg">
      <col gap="sm" h="fill" justify="center">
        <text variant="kicker" color="muted">python-pptx</text>
        <text role="title" size="168" color="accent5">128<span size="48"> times</span></text>
        <text role="heading" size="28">Manual coordinates · 10 raw-XML patches</text>
        <shape type="rect" fill="pattern(vertical accent5/70 bg/0)" border="none" w="fill" h="20"/>
      </col>
    </shape>
    <shape type="rounded-rect" fill="gradient(accent1 accent6, 135deg)" border="none" radius="lg" shadow="soft" w="fill" pad="lg">
      <col gap="md" h="fill" justify="center">
        <text variant="kicker" color="bg">balpyo</text>
        <text role="title" size="104" color="bg">1<span size="48"> line</span></text>
        <shape type="rounded-rect" fill="alpha(bg, 0.2)" border="none" radius="sm" pad="xs sm">
          <text role="code" size="22" color="bg">&lt;grid cols="4"&gt;</text>
        </shape>
        <text role="body" color="bg">The browser measures layout.</text>
      </col>
    </shape>
  </grid>
  <note>This is where the product started. If the author still has something to calculate, it isn't automation.</note>
</slide>
